# English — the source language of the interface.
#
# Every user-facing string in crates/ui/*.slint is written in English inside
# `@tr("…")`, so this catalog is deliberately empty: no msgid needs a translation,
# and a missing entry makes Slint fall back to the source text (which *is* the
# English string). The header is still required — slint-build refuses to compile
# when `translations/` holds no catalog, and this one is what registers "en" as a
# bundled language so `slint::select_bundled_translation("en")` (the English
# entry of Settings → Display) succeeds instead of erroring.
#
# To add a language: create translations/<code>/LC_MESSAGES/nova-ui.po next to this
# file, add the matching `nova_config::Language` variant, and generate the catalog
# entries with `slint-tr-extractor --no-default-translation-context` (the
# catalogs are context-free — see crates/ui/build.rs); entries start as
# msgid-only, so untranslated strings keep showing English.
